    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Hegarty Properties proudly presents No. 10 Sea View Park, a charming 2-bedroom detached bungalow nestled within a quiet and mature residential development in the picturesque coastal village of Ballycotton, Co. Cork. Enjoying a private, south- easterly facing site, this home is filled with natural light and offers a peaceful atmosphere, making it an ideal permanent residence, retirement home or coastal holiday retreat.\r\nOutside, the property enjoys private, low-maintenance gardens with a desirable south-easterly orientation, providing a peaceful setting to enjoy the sunshine throughout the day. Ample off-street parking is available to the front. \r\nIdeally located adjacent to Ballycotton Pitch & Putt Club and just a short stroll from the vibrant village of Ballycotton, residents can enjoy an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants and traditional pubs, together with Ballycotton Harbour, the famous Cliff Walk and nearby beaches. The renowned Ballymaloe House and Cookery School, along with the many attractions of East Cork, are all within easy reach.\r\nCombining a peaceful setting with an enviable coastal location, No. 10 Sea View Park presents a wonderful opportunity to acquire a detached home in one of East Cork's most desirable seaside villages.\r\nAccommodation includes: Entrance Porch & Hallway, Sitting Room, Kitchen/Dining Area, 2 Bedrooms (1 Ensuite) and Family Bathroom. (Approx. 60 sq. m. / 645 sq. ft.)\r\n\r\nGuide Price: €325,000"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Porch:\t\t\tPorch with tiled floor leading to hall.\r\n\r\nHall:\t\t\tFeatures Lino flooring. \r\n\r\nSitting Room:             Front aspect with open fireplace and lino flooring.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Area: The kitchen features a fitted kitchen with electric cooker, free-standing fridge and washing machine. Double doors to rear garden and lino flooring. \r\n\r\n\r\nBedroom 1:\tDouble room with lino flooring.  \r\n\r\nEnsuite:\tW.C., wash hand basin & electric shower.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2:\tDouble room with lino flooring. \r\n\r\nBathroom:                     W.C., W.H.B. & Bath. \r\n\r\nServices:\tO.F.C.H.\tMains Sewerage. \tMains Water. \r\n\r\nOutside: \tSuperbly positioned with a desirable south-easterly orientation, the property enjoys low-maintenance gardens to the front and rear, predominantly laid in gravel with mature hedging and established specimen planting. The front garden provides ample off-street parking, while the enclosed rear garden offers a peaceful outdoor space."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tBuilt in 1996\r\n•\tBER: C \tBER Number: 119698462\r\n•\tDouble-glazed P.V.C. windows. \r\n•\tLocated in a quiet, mature and highly sought-after residential development\r\n•\tLow-maintenance gardens with mature planting\r\n•\tAmple off-street parking\r\n•\tAdjacent to Ballycotton Pitch & Putt Club\r\n•\tWalking distance to Ballycotton village, harbour, Cliff Walk, beach and local amenities\r\n•\tExcellent investment opportunity in a prime coastal location\r\n•\tEircode:  P25 K099"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: C"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Directions",
        "SortOrder": 5,
